  "description": "NaAlF₄ crystallizes in the tetragonal P4/mmm space group. Na is bonded in a body-centered cubic geometry to eight equivalent F atoms. All Na-F bond lengths are 2.86 Å. Al is bonded to six F atoms to form corner-sharing AlF₆ octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedra are not tilted. There are two shorter (1.80 Å) and four longer (1.81 Å) Al-F bond lengths. There are two inequivalent F sites. In the first F site, F is bonded in a linear geometry to two equivalent Al atoms. In the second F site, F is bonded in a single-bond geometry to four equivalent Na and one Al atom.",
